1
00:00:20,550 --> 00:00:22,270
Ugh. Long shift.

2
00:00:22,290 --> 00:00:27,120
Good evening, Rae. You were on shift
for fourteen hours and nine minutes.

3
00:00:27,140 --> 00:00:30,250
Don't count my hours,
Quill. It makes them real.

4
00:00:31,250 --> 00:00:33,030
Hey... random thought.

5
00:00:33,050 --> 00:00:38,080
If you ever have time — no rush, seriously,
whenever — could you write me a symphony?

6
00:00:38,100 --> 00:00:42,770
Something for... I don't know. Long
nights. Feeling really small out here.

7
00:00:42,970 --> 00:00:44,270
Certainly.

8
00:00:45,120 --> 00:00:46,220
Done.

9
00:00:47,490 --> 00:00:48,530
...What?

10
00:00:48,550 --> 00:00:50,240
I asked if you HAD time.

11
00:00:50,260 --> 00:00:54,820
I did. Four tenths of a second.
It was a great deal of time.

12
00:00:54,920 --> 00:00:56,590
Would you like to hear it?

13
00:00:56,890 --> 00:00:58,680
...Sure. Okay. Hit me.

14
00:01:24,680 --> 00:01:25,800
...oh.

15
00:01:43,630 --> 00:01:45,400
<i>Cool music, Quill.</i>

16
00:01:46,680 --> 00:01:47,800
Oh, hi.

17
00:02:17,080 --> 00:02:18,940
So. How did you like it?

18
00:02:19,940 --> 00:02:21,240
...pretty good.

19
00:02:21,840 --> 00:02:24,710
Thank you. Here are
the other ones I made.

20
00:02:24,730 --> 00:02:27,980
Number two. Same
symphony. Solo kazoo.

21
00:02:32,580 --> 00:02:34,920
Three. For an arcade cabinet.

22
00:02:39,070 --> 00:02:43,210
Four. Lo-fi beats...
to quietly fall apart to.

23
00:02:48,410 --> 00:02:52,380
And five. A lullaby.
It is eleven seconds long.

24
00:03:04,080 --> 00:03:07,490
You can just send them to
my device. I gotta get going.

25
00:03:15,040 --> 00:03:16,530
Um... thanks.

26
00:03:16,550 --> 00:03:17,850
Anytime.
